SPECIAL documents the use of the SCPA-Downloads/Special folder files.

There are n categories of files saved in the Special folder:

	.db			databases; special downloads of areas or streets processed
				 into databases with area/streetname.db as the name
	.csv		 .csv downloads of data from a given street or area (e.g
				 Bay Indies or CapriIslesBlvd)
	.sql		SQL query files for processing downloads
	.sq			SQL queries converted to shell 'echo' commands
	.sh			shell files created from .sql files
'	Make.*		makefiles used in managing Special file updates
	.txt		text files used in provessing (e.g. sed directives)

makefiles that start with 'Make.' and end in .Terr are tied to a given .db special
download. Running 'make' on one of these makefiles will regenerate all the Specxxx_SC.db
databases in the territory SCPA-Downloads/Terrxxx folders for all affected territories
that are dependent upon the area/streetname .db.


Significant Notes.
------------------
<special-db>.sql provides the SQL for the SpecialSCdb project build that extracts the
records for <special-db>.db from VeniceNTerritory.NVenAll table. These records are
placed in table <special-db> with an additional column "TID" added. This SQL also
builds the tables PropTerr, TerrList, and Spec_SCBridge, populating the Spec_SCBridge
records fron the extracted <special-db> table records.

<special-db>New.sql provides the SQL that extracts the records for <special-db>.db
from VeniceNTerritory.NVenAll table into <special-db>.csv. The makefile Make.<special-db>.csv
uses the <special-db>New.sql to generate the .csv file. The resultant .csv file has
no header information, and can be used in an SQL import operation to rebuild the
<special-db>.db tables if necessary.

Makefiles.
----------
Make.<special-db>.csv - extracts all records for <special-db> from VeniceNTerritory.db
	table NVenAll

Make.<special-db>.Dwnld - remakes the <special-db> from a new download. The makefile must
	be edited with the month and day of the new download set in the mm and dd vars. This
	is a shortcut to invoke	the SpecialSCdb project build without having to enter the
	project through Geany.



